#: installation_old.md:1
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "インストール"

#: installation_old.md:3
msgid ""
"In this page you can learn how to configure, compile and install PLUMED."
msgstr "このページで設定・ビルド・インストールを学びます。"

#: installation_old.md:5
msgid "For those of you who are impatient, the following might do the job:"
msgstr "手短には次で十分かもしれません。"

#: installation_old.md:14
msgid ""
"Notice that `make install` is not strictly necessary as plumed can be used "
"from the compilation directory. This is very useful so as to quickly test "
"the implementation of new features. However, we strongly recommend to "
"perform a full install."
msgstr ""
"ビルド先から使えるので `make install` は厳密には不要で、新機能の素早いテストに便利です。ただし完全なインストールを強く推奨します。"

#: installation_old.md:18
msgid ""
"Once the above is completed the `plumed` executable should be in your "
"execution path and you will be able to use PLUMED to analyze existing "
"trajectories or play with the Lennard-Jones code that is included. You "
"should even be able to use it with some MD codes that include PLUMED within "
"them. As explained below, however, with some other MD codes you will need to"
" patch them with PLUMED before compilation. Again, if you are impatient, "
"something like this will do this job in many cases:"
msgstr ""
"`plumed` が PATH に入り、Trajectory 解析や内蔵 Lennard-Jones コードを使えます。組み込み対応 MD "
"でも使えますが、別途 Patch が必要なものもあります。多くは次で行えます。"

#: installation_old.md:31
msgid ""
"After running this command you then compile your MD code. For some MD codes "
"these instructions are insufficient. It is thus recommended that you read "
"the instructions at the end of this page. Notice that MD codes could in "
"principle be \"PLUMED ready\" in their official distribution. If your "
"favorite MD code is available \"PLUMED ready\" you will have to compile "
"PLUMED first, then (optionally) install it, then check the MD codes' manual "
"to discover how to link it."
msgstr ""
"この後 MD をコンパイルします。不十分なコードもあるので末尾を参照してください。公式に PLUMED Ready の MD なら、先に PLUMED "
"をビルドし、任意でインストール後、MD マニュアルの Link 手順に従います。"

#: installation_old.md:40
msgid "Supported compilers"
msgstr "対応 Compiler"

#: installation_old.md:42
msgid "As of PLUMED 2.10, we require a compiler that supports C++17."
msgstr "PLUMED 2.10から C++17 対応が必要です。"

#: installation_old.md:44
msgid ""
"Notice that the `./configure` script verifies that your compiler supports "
"C++17. Some compilers do not declare full support, but implement anyway a "
"number of C++17 features sufficient to compile PLUMED. In case you see a "
"warning about C++17 support during `./configure` please make sure that "
"PLUMED compiles correctly and, if possible, execute the regtests (using "
"`make regtest`). Notice that we regularly test a number of compilers on "
"travis-ci, and at least those compilers are guaranteed to be able to compile"
" PLUMED correctly."
msgstr ""
"`./configure` が C++17 を確認します。完全対応を宣言しなくても必要機能がある Compiler "
"もあります。`./configure` で警告が出たら、正しいビルドと、可能なら `make regtest` を確認します。travis-ci "
"で定期テストする Compiler はビルドできることを保証します。"

#: installation_old.md:52
msgid "Configuring PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED の構成設定"

#: installation_old.md:54
msgid ""
"The `./configure` command just generates a Makefile.conf file and a "
"sourceme.sh file. In PLUMED 2.0 these files were prepared and stored in the "
"directory configurations/. The new ones generated by ./configure are similar"
" to the old ones but are not completely compatible. In particular, some of "
"the -D options have been changed in version 2.2, and several new variables "
"so as to specify the installation directories have been added. For this "
"reason, you now should run `./configure` again. Anyway, it should be easy to"
" enforce a similar setup with autoconf by passing the proper arguments on "
"the command line. If you have problems on your architecture, please report "
"them to the mailing list."
msgstr ""
"`./configure` は Makefile.conf と sourceme.sh を作ります。2.0では configurations/ "
"に事前配置していましたが、新版とは完全互換ではありません。2.2で -D が変わり、インストール先の変数も増えたため、`./configure` "
"を再実行してください。適切な引数で旧設定を再現できるはずです。問題は Mailing List に報告してください。"

#: installation_old.md:67
msgid "Useful command line options for `./configure` can be found by typing"
msgstr "`./configure` の便利なオプションは、"

#: installation_old.md:73
msgid ""
"PLUMED is made up of modules. Some of them are on by default, some others "
"aren't. Since version 2.3, the activation of modules should be made during "
"configuration using the `--enable-modules` option."
msgstr "Module は既定有効・無効に分かれ、2.3以降は `--enable-modules` で設定時に選びます。"

#: installation_old.md:77
msgid ""
"Notice that some of the methods within PLUMED depend on external libraries "
"which are looked for by configure. You can typically avoid looking for a "
"library using the \"disable\" syntax, e.g."
msgstr "一部は configure が探す外部 Library に依存します。通常 disable で探索を止められます。"

#: installation_old.md:85
msgid ""
"Notice that when MPI search is enabled (by default) compilers such as "
"\"mpic++\" and \"mpicxx\" are searched for first. On the other hand, if MPI "
"search is disabled (\"./configure --disable-mpi\") non-mpi compilers are "
"searched for. Notice that only a few of the possible compiler name are "
"searched. Thus, compilers such as \"g++-mp-4.8\" should be explicitly "
"requested with the CXX option."
msgstr ""
"MPI 探索は既定で有効で mpic++・mpicxx を優先します。./configure --disable-mpi なら非 MPI "
"Compiler を探します。探索名は限られるため、g++-mp-4.8 などは CXX で明示します。"

#: installation_old.md:92
msgid ""
"You can better control which compiler is used by setting the variables CXX "
"and CC. E.g., to use Intel compilers use the following command:"
msgstr "CXX・CC で Compiler を制御できます。Intel の例は、"

#: installation_old.md:99
msgid ""
"Notice that we are using icpc in this example, which is not an MPI compiler "
"as a result MPI will not be enabled. Also consider that this is different "
"with respect to what some other configure script does in that variables such"
" as MPICXX are completely ignored here. In case you work on a machine where "
"CXX is set to a serial compiler and MPICXX to a MPI compiler, to compile "
"with MPI you should use"
msgstr ""
"icpc は MPI Compiler でないため、MPI は無効です。ほかの configure と違い MPICXX は無視します。CXX "
"が逐次、MPICXX が MPI なら、次を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:110
msgid ""
"[!warning] This procedure could be somehow confusing since many other "
"programs behave in a different way. The flag `--enable-mpi` is perfectly "
"valid but is not needed here. Autoconf will check if a code containing MPI "
"calls can be compiled, and if so it will enable it. `--disable-mpi` could be"
" used if you are using a compiler that supports MPI but you don't want "
"PLUMED to be compiled with MPI support. Thus the correct way to enable MPI "
"is to pass to ./configure the name of a C++ compiler that implements MPI "
"using the CXX option. In this way, MPI library is treated similarly to all "
"the other libraries that PLUMED tries to link by default."
msgstr ""
"[!warning] 他プログラムと違うため注意してください。`--enable-mpi` は有効ですが不要です。MPI "
"呼び出しをコンパイルできれば自動有効化します。対応 Compiler でも無効にするなら `--disable-mpi` です。CXX で MPI "
"C++ Compiler を渡すのが正しい方法で、他 Library と同様に扱います。"

#: installation_old.md:121
msgid "To tune the compilation options you can use the CXXFLAGS variable:"
msgstr "CXXFLAGS でオプションを調整します。"

#: installation_old.md:127
msgid ""
"If you are implementing new functionality and want to build with debug flags"
" in place so as to do some checking you can use"
msgstr "新機能の Debug 確認には、"

#: installation_old.md:134
msgid ""
"This will perform some extra check during execution (possibly slowing down "
"PLUMED) and write full symbol tables in the executable (making the final "
"executable much larger)."
msgstr "実行時の追加検査で遅くなり、完全な Symbol Table で実行ファイルも大きくなります。"

#: installation_old.md:137
msgid ""
"The main goal of the automatic configure is to find the libraries. When they"
" are stored in unconventional places it is thus sensible to tell autoconf "
"where to look! To do this there are some environment variable that can be "
"used to instruct the linker which directories it should search for libraries"
" inside. These variables are compiler dependent, but could have been set by "
"the system administrator so that libraries are found without any extra flag."
" Our suggested procedure is to first try to configure without any additional"
" flags and to then check the log so as to see whether or not the libraries "
"were properly detected."
msgstr ""
"configure の主目的は Library 探索です。標準外の場所は環境変数で Linker に伝えます。Compiler "
"依存で、管理者が設定済みの場合もあります。まず追加 Flag なしで試し、Log で検出結果を確認してください。"

#: installation_old.md:146
msgid ""
"If a library is not found during configuration, you can try to use options "
"to modify the search path. For example if your gsl libraries is in "
"`/opt/local` (this is where MacPorts put it) and configure is not able to "
"find it you can try"
msgstr "見つからなければ探索 Path を変更します。例えば MacPorts の GSL が `/opt/local` にあるなら、"

#: installation_old.md:155
msgid ""
"Notice that PLUMED will first try to link a routine from say gsl without any"
" additional flag, and then in case of failure will retry adding \"-lgsl\" to"
" the LIBS options. If also this does not work, the gsl library will be "
"disabled and some features will not be available. This procedure allows you "
"to use libraries with custom names. So, if your gsl library is called "
"`/opt/local/lib/libmygsl.so` you can link it with"
msgstr ""
"まず Flag なし、次に LIBS に -lgsl を加えて試し、失敗すると GSL "
"を無効にします。独自名にも対応し、`/opt/local/lib/libmygsl.so` なら、"

#: installation_old.md:169
msgid ""
"In this example, the linker will directly try to link "
"`/opt/local/lib/libmygsl.so`. This rule is true for all the libraries, so "
"that you will always be able to link a specific version of a library by "
"specifying it using the LIBS variable."
msgstr ""
"直接 `/opt/local/lib/libmygsl.so` に Link します。全 Library に同じ規則が使え、LIBS "
"で特定版を明示できます。"

#: installation_old.md:173
msgid ""
"Since version 2.3.2, the search for the library functions passing to the "
"linker a flag with the standard library name (in the gsl example, it would "
"be `-lgsl`) can be skipped by using the option `--disable-libsearch`. Notice"
" that in this manner only libraries that are explicitly passed using the "
"`LIBS` option will be linked. For instance"
msgstr ""
"2.3.2以降は `--disable-libsearch` で標準名（例：`-lgsl`）の探索を省き、`LIBS` に明示したものだけ Link "
"できます。例えば、"

#: installation_old.md:181
msgid ""
"will make sure that only gsl is linked and, for instance, BLAS and LAPACK "
"libraries are not. This might be useful when installing PLUMED within "
"package managers such as MacPorts to make sure that only desired libraries "
"are linked and thus to avoid to introduce spurious dependencies. The only "
"exception to this rule is `-ldl`, which is anyway a system library on Linux."
msgstr ""
"GSL だけを Link し BLAS・LAPACK は使いません。Package Manager で不要な依存を防ぐのに便利です。Linux "
"System Library の `-ldl` は例外です。"

#: installation_old.md:186
msgid ""
"[!warning] On OSX it is common practice to hard code the full path to "
"libraries in the libraries themselves. This means that, after having linked "
"a shared library, that specific shared library will be searched in the same "
"place (we do the same for the `libplumed.dylib` library, which has an "
"install name hard coded). On the other hand, on Linux it is common practice "
"not to hard code the full path. This means that if you use the `LDFLAGS` "
"option to specify the path to the libraries you want to link to PLUMED (e.g."
" `./configure LDFLAGS=\"-L/path\"`) these libraries might not be found "
"later. The visible symptom is that `src/lib/plumed-shared` will not be "
"linked correctly. Although the file 'src/lib/plumed-shared' is not "
"necessary, being able to produce it means that it will be possible to link "
"PLUMED dynamically with MD codes later."
msgstr ""
"[!warning] OSX は Library に絶対 Path を固定するのが一般的で、Link "
"後も同じ場所を探します（`libplumed.dylib` も同様）。Linux は通常固定せず、`LDFLAGS` "
"で指定しても後で見つからない場合があります（例：`./configure LDFLAGS=\"-L/path\"`）。症状は "
"`src/lib/plumed-shared` の Link 失敗です。これは必須でないものの、作れれば MD と Dynamic Link "
"できることを示します。"

#: installation_old.md:200
msgid ""
"The easiest solution to this problem is to hard code the library search path"
" in this way:"
msgstr "最も簡単なのは、次のように Library 探索 Path を固定する方法です。"

#: installation_old.md:206
msgid ""
"Notice that as of PLUMED v2.4 it is possible to use the configure option "
"`--enable-rpath` to automatically hard code the path defined in "
"`LIBRARY_PATH`:"
msgstr "v2.4以降は `--enable-rpath` で `LIBRARY_PATH` を自動的に固定できます。"

#: installation_old.md:213
msgid ""
"In this way, the search path used at link time (`LIBRARY_PATH`) and the one "
"saved in the `libplumed.so` library will be consistent by construction. In a"
" typical environment configured using module framework "
"(http://modules.sourceforge.net), `LIBRARY_PATH` will be a variable "
"containing the path to all the modules loaded at compilation time."
msgstr ""
"Link 時の `LIBRARY_PATH` と `libplumed.so` の保存 Path が一致します。Environment Modules "
"(http://modules.sourceforge.net) では通常、`LIBRARY_PATH` にビルド時の全 Module の Path "
"が入っています。"

#: installation_old.md:219
msgid ""
"PLUMED needs BLAS and LAPACK. These are treated slightly different from "
"other libraries. The search is done in the usual way (i.e., first look for "
"them without any link flag, then add \"-lblas\" and \"-llapack\", "
"respectively). As such if you want to use a specific version of BLAS or "
"LAPACK you can make them available to configure by using"
msgstr "BLAS・LAPACK は必須で、通常どおり Flag なし、次に -lblas・-llapack で探します。特定版は次で指定できます。"

#: installation_old.md:229
msgid ""
"If the functions of these libraries are not found, the compiler looks for a "
"version with a final underscore added. Finally, since BLAS and LAPACK are "
"compulsory in PLUMED, you can use a internal version of these libraries that"
" comes as part of PLUMED. If all else fails the internal version of BLAS and"
" LAPACK are the ones that will be used by PLUMED. If you wish to disable any"
" search for external libraries (e.g. because the system libraries have "
"problems) this can be done with"
msgstr ""
"関数がなければ末尾 Underscore 付きも探します。必須なので、最後には同梱の Internal 版を使います。System Library "
"に問題があるなど、外部探索を完全に止めるには、"

#: installation_old.md:242
msgid ""
"Notice that you can also disable external LAPACK only, that is use internal "
"LAPACK with external BLAS using"
msgstr "External LAPACK だけ止め、Internal LAPACK と External BLAS も使えます。"

#: installation_old.md:249
msgid ""
"Since typically it is the BLAS library that can be heavily optimized, this "
"configuration should not provide significant slowing down and could be used "
"on systems where native LAPACK libraries have problems."
msgstr "主に最適化が効くのは BLAS なので、大幅には遅くならず、Native LAPACK に問題がある系に使えます。"

#: installation_old.md:253
msgid ""
"As a final resort, you can also edit the resulting Makefile.conf file. "
"Notable variables in this file include:"
msgstr "最終手段は Makefile.conf の編集です。主な変数は、"

#: installation_old.md:255
msgid ""
"`DYNAMIC_LIB` : these are the libraries needed to compile the PLUMED library"
" (e.g. `-L/path/to/gsl -lgsl` etc). Notice that for the PLUMED shared "
"library to be compiled properly these should be dynamic libraries. Also "
"notice that PLUMED preferentially requires BLAS and LAPACK library. Notice "
"that the variables that you supply with `configure LIBS=something` will end "
"up in this variable. This is a bit misleading but is required to keep the "
"configuration files compatible with PLUMED 2.0."
msgstr ""
"`DYNAMIC_LIB`：PLUMED Library の依存（例：`-L/path/to/gsl -lgsl`）。Shared 版には "
"Dynamic Library が必要で、BLAS・LAPACK を優先します。`configure LIBS=something` "
"もここに入り、紛らわしいですが2.0互換のためです。"

#: installation_old.md:262
msgid ""
"`LIBS` : these are the libraries needed when patching an MD code; typically "
"only \"-ldl\" (needed to have functions for dynamic loading)."
msgstr "`LIBS`：MD Patch の依存。通常 Dynamic Loading 用の -ldl のみ。"

#: installation_old.md:263
msgid ""
"`CPPFLAGS` : add here definition needed to enable specific optional "
"functions; e.g. use `-D__PLUMED_HAS_GSL` to enable the gsl library"
msgstr "`CPPFLAGS`：追加機能の定義。例えば `-D__PLUMED_HAS_GSL` で GSL を有効化する。"

#: installation_old.md:265
msgid ""
"`SOEXT` : this gives the extension for shared libraries in your system, "
"typically \"so\" on UNIX, \"dylib\" on mac; If your system does not support "
"dynamic libraries or, for some other reason, you would like a static "
"executable you can just set this variable to a blank (\"SOEXT=\")."
msgstr ""
"`SOEXT`：Shared Library 拡張子（UNIX は so、Mac は dylib）。非対応または Static を望むなら空の "
"SOEXT= にする。"

#: installation_old.md:269
msgid "BLAS and LAPACK"
msgstr "BLAS と LAPACK"

#: installation_old.md:271
msgid ""
"We tried to keep PLUMED as independent as possible from external libraries "
"and as such those features that require external libraries are optional. "
"However, to have a properly working version of plumed PLUMED you need BLAS "
"and LAPACK libraries. We would strongly recommend you download these "
"libraries and install them separately so as to have the most efficient "
"possible implementations of the functions contained within them. However, if"
" you cannot install BLAS and LAPACK, you can use the internal ones. Since "
"version 2.1, PLUMED uses a configure script to detect libraries. In case "
"system LAPACK or BLAS are not found on your system, PLUMED will use the "
"internal replacement."
msgstr ""
"外部依存はできる限り Optional にしていますが、BLAS・LAPACK は必須です。効率的な実装を別途入れることを強く推奨します。無理なら "
"Internal 版を使えます。2.1以降 configure が System 版を検出し、なければ Internal に切り替えます。"

#: installation_old.md:279
msgid ""
"We have had a number of emails (and have struggled ourselves) with ensuring "
"that PLUMED can link BLAS and LAPACK. The following describes some of the "
"pitfalls that you can fall into and a set of sensible steps by which you can"
" check whether or not you have set up the configuration correctly."
msgstr "Link に関する相談は多く、私たちも苦労しました。落とし穴と確認手順を示します。"

#: installation_old.md:284
msgid ""
"Notice first of all that the `DYNAMIC_LIB` variable in the Makefile.conf "
"should contain the flag necessary to load the BLAS and LAPACK libraries. "
"Typically this will be `-llapack -lblas`, in some case followed by "
"`-lgfortran`. Full path specification with `-L` may be necessary and on some"
" machines the BLAS and LAPACK libraries may not be called `-llapack` and "
"`-lblas`. Everything will depend on your system configuration."
msgstr ""
"Makefile.conf の `DYNAMIC_LIB` に必要な Flag（通常 `-llapack -lblas`、時に "
"`-lgfortran`）が必要です。`-L` による絶対 Path や、`-llapack`・`-lblas` 以外の名前が必要な系もあります。"

#: installation_old.md:290
msgid "Some simple to fix further problems include:"
msgstr "ほかの簡単な対策は、"

#: installation_old.md:291
msgid ""
"If the linker complains and suggests recompiling LAPACK with `-fPIC`, it "
"means that you have static LAPACK libraries. Either install dynamic LAPACK "
"libraries or switch to static compilation of PLUMED by stopping to set the "
"SOEXT variable in the configuration file."
msgstr ""
"`-fPIC` で LAPACK を再ビルドせよと出るなら Static 版です。Dynamic 版を入れるか、SOEXT を設定せず PLUMED を"
" Static にします。"

#: installation_old.md:294
msgid ""
"If the linker complains about other missing functions (typically starting "
"with \"for_\" prefix) then you should also link some Fortran libraries. "
"PLUMED is written in C++ and often C++ linkers do not include Fortran "
"libraries by default. These libraries are required for LAPACK and BLAS to "
"work. Please check the documentation of your compiler."
msgstr ""
"for_ などの関数がないなら Fortran Library も Link します。C++ Linker は通常自動では含めません。Compiler "
"の説明を参照してください。"

#: installation_old.md:298
msgid ""
"If the linker complains that dsyevr_ cannot be found, try adding "
"`-DF77_NO_UNDERSCORE` to CPPFLAGS Notice that \"./configure\" should "
"automatically try this solution."
msgstr ""
"dsyevr_ がなければ CPPFLAGS に `-DF77_NO_UNDERSCORE` を試します。configure も自動的に試すはずです。"

#: installation_old.md:302
msgid "VMD trajectory plugins"
msgstr "VMD Trajectory Plugin"

#: installation_old.md:304
msgid ""
"PLUMED source code already includes a few selected VMD molfile plugins so as"
" to read a small number of additional trajectory formats (e.g., dcd, gromacs"
" files, pdb, and amber files). If you configure PLUMED with the full set of "
"VMD plugins you will be able to read many more trajectory formats, basically"
" all of those supported by VMD. To this aim, you need to download the SOURCE"
" of VMD, which contains a plugins directory. Adapt build.sh and compile it. "
"At the end, you should get the molfile plugins compiled as a static library "
"`libmolfile_plugin.a`. Locate said file and `libmolfile_plugin.h`, they "
"should be in a directory called `/pathtovmdplugins/ARCH/molfile` (e.g. "
"`/pathtovmdplugins/MACOSXX86_64/molfile`). Also locate file "
"`molfile_plugin.h`, which should be in `/pathtovmdplugins/include`. Then "
"customize the configure command with something along the lines of:"
msgstr ""
"dcd、GROMACS、pdb、AMBER 用の一部は同梱です。全形式には VMD Source の plugins を取得し、build.sh "
"を調整してビルドします。`libmolfile_plugin.a` と `libmolfile_plugin.h` は "
"`/pathtovmdplugins/ARCH/molfile`（例：`/pathtovmdplugins/MACOSXX86_64/molfile`）、`molfile_plugin.h`"
" は `/pathtovmdplugins/include` にあります。configure を次のように調整します。"

#: installation_old.md:322
msgid ""
"Notice that it might be necessary to add to `LDFLAGS` the path to your TCL "
"interpreter, e.g."
msgstr "TCL Interpreter の Path を `LDFLAGS` に加える場合もあります。"

#: installation_old.md:329
msgid "Then, rebuild plumed."
msgstr "その後 PLUMED を再ビルドします。"

#: installation_old.md:331
msgid "Configure PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED の設定"

#: installation_old.md:333
msgid ""
"Once the environment variables are set, we can configure PLUMED with the "
"`--enable-libtorch` keyword:"
msgstr "環境変数を設定したら `--enable-libtorch` を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:339
msgid "**Notes**"
msgstr "**注**"

#: installation_old.md:340
msgid ""
"In order to activate the [PYTORCH module](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/module_pytorch/) one needs to add `--enable-"
"modules=pytorch` or `--enable-modules=all`."
msgstr ""
"[PYTORCH Module](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/module_pytorch/) には `--enable-modules=pytorch` または `--enable-"
"modules=all` が必要です。"

#: installation_old.md:341
msgid ""
"`--enable-libtorch` will first try first to link the CUDA-enabled library "
"and if it does not found it will try to link the CPU-only version."
msgstr "`--enable-libtorch` はまず CUDA 版、なければ CPU-only を試します。"

#: installation_old.md:342
msgid ""
"To verify that the linking of LibTorch is succesful, one should look at the "
"output of the configure commands: `checking libtorch[cpu/cuda] [without "
"extra libs/with -ltorch_cpu ... ]`. If any of these commands are succesfull,"
" it will return `... yes`. Otherwise, the configure will display a warning "
"(and not an error!) that says: `configure: WARNING: cannot enable "
"__PLUMED_HAS_LIBTORCH`. In this case, it is recommended to examine the "
"output of the above commands in the config.log file to understand the reason"
" (e.g. it cannot find the required libraries)."
msgstr ""
"出力の `checking libtorch[cpu/cuda] [without extra libs/with -ltorch_cpu ... ]`"
" を見て、いずれかが `... yes` なら成功です。失敗はエラーでなく `configure: WARNING: cannot enable "
"__PLUMED_HAS_LIBTORCH` という警告です。config.log で原因（Library が見つからないなど）を確認してください。"

#: installation_old.md:343
msgid ""
"If you want to use the pre-cxx11 ABI LibTorch binaries (useful for instance "
"when installing it on an HPC cluster) then you should download the related "
"version from PyTorch website (e.g. <a "
"href=\"https://download.pytorch.org/libtorch/cpu/libtorch-shared-with-"
"deps-2.0.0%2Bcpu.zip\"> `libtorch-shared-with-deps-2.0.0%2Bcpu.zip`</a>) and"
" add the following option to the configure: "
"`CXXFLAGS=\"-D_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0\"`."
msgstr ""
"HPC などで Pre-cxx11 ABI Binary を使うなら、PyTorch の対応版（例：<a "
"href=\"https://download.pytorch.org/libtorch/cpu/libtorch-shared-with-"
"deps-2.0.0%2Bcpu.zip\"> `libtorch-shared-with-"
"deps-2.0.0%2Bcpu.zip`</a>）を取得し、`CXXFLAGS=\"-D_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0\"` "
"を加えます。"

#: installation_old.md:345
msgid "Additional Modules"
msgstr "追加 Module"

#: installation_old.md:347
msgid ""
"PLUMED includes some additional modules that by default are not compiled, "
"but can be enabled during configuration. You can use the option `--enable-"
"modules` to activate some of them, e.g."
msgstr "既定で無効の Module は `--enable-modules` で有効化できます。例えば、"

#: installation_old.md:354
msgid ""
"For more information on modules see [the modules "
"page](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/modules/)."
msgstr ""
"詳細は [Module 一覧](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/modules/) "
"を参照してください。"

#: installation_old.md:356
msgid "Compiling PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED のコンパイル"

#: installation_old.md:358
msgid "Once configured, PLUMED can be compiled using the following command:"
msgstr "設定後、次でコンパイルします。"

#: installation_old.md:364
msgid ""
"This will compile the entire code and produce a number of files in the "
"'src/lib' directory, including the executable 'src/lib/plumed'. When shared "
"libraries are enabled, a shared libraries called 'src/lib/libKernel.so' "
"should also be present. Notice that the extension could be '.dylib' on a "
"Mac."
msgstr ""
"src/lib に全コードをビルドし、src/lib/plumed などを生成します。Shared 有効なら "
"src/lib/libKernel.so、Mac なら .dylib もあります。"

#: installation_old.md:370
msgid ""
"In case you want to run PLUMED *without installing it* (i.e. from the "
"compilation directory), you can use the file 'sourceme.sh' that has been "
"created by the configure script in the main PLUMED directory. This file can "
"be \"sourced\" (presently only working for bash shell) if you want to use "
"PLUMED *before installing it* (i.e. from the compilation directory). It is a"
" good idea to source it now, so that you can play with the just compiled "
"PLUMED:"
msgstr ""
"_インストールせず_ ビルド先から使うには、Main の sourceme.sh を Source します。現在 Bash のみです。_インストール前_"
" の実行に使い、今も Source して試せます。"

#: installation_old.md:382
msgid "Now a \"plumed\" executable should be in your path. Try to type"
msgstr "plumed が PATH に入り、次を実行できます。"

#: installation_old.md:388
msgid ""
"[!warning] If you are cross compiling, the plumed executable will not work. "
"As a consequence, you won't be able to run regtests or compile the manual. "
"This is not a problem."
msgstr ""
"[!warning] Cross-compile の実行ファイルはビルド先で動かず、Regression Test "
"やマニュアル作成はできませんが、問題ありません。"

#: installation_old.md:393
msgid ""
"You can also check if PLUMED is correctly compiled by performing our "
"regression tests. Be warned that some of them fail because of the different "
"numerical accuracy on different machines. As of version 2.4, in order to "
"test the `plumed` executable that you just compiled (prior to installing it)"
" you can use the following command"
msgstr ""
"Regression Test で確認できます。マシン間の数値精度差で失敗するものもあります。2.4以降、インストール前の `plumed` "
"は次でテストします。"

#: installation_old.md:402
msgid ""
"On the other hand, in order to test the `plumed` executable that you just "
"installed you should type"
msgstr "インストール済み `plumed` は、"

#: installation_old.md:409
msgid ""
"In addition, similarly to previous versions of PLUMED, you can test the "
"`plumed` executable that is in your current path with"
msgstr "現在 PATH にある `plumed` は、"

#: installation_old.md:417
msgid "You can check the exact version they will use by using the command"
msgstr "使用する厳密な版は次で確認します。"

#: installation_old.md:423
msgid ""
"Thus, you can easily run the test suite using a different version of PLUMED "
"(maybe an earlier version that you already installed), just making sure that"
" it can be found in the path. Clearly, if you test a given version of PLUMED"
" with a test suite from a different version you can expect two possible "
"kinds of innocuous errors:"
msgstr ""
"PATH を変えれば旧版など別の PLUMED もテストできます。ただし Test Suite と版が違う場合、2種類の問題のないエラーがあり得ます。"

#: installation_old.md:428
msgid ""
"If `plumed` executable is older than the test suite, the tests might fail "
"since they rely on some feature introduced in PLUMED in a newer version."
msgstr "`plumed` が古いと新機能がなく失敗する。"

#: installation_old.md:430
msgid ""
"If `plumed` executable is newer than the test suite, the tests might fail "
"since some non-backward compatible change was made in PLUMED. We try to keep"
" the number of non-backward compatible changes small, but as you can see "
"from the change log that there are typically a few of them at every new "
"major release."
msgstr "`plumed` が新しいと非互換変更で失敗する。数は抑えていますが、各 Major Release に多少あります。"

#: installation_old.md:436
msgid ""
"[!attention] Even though we regularly perform tests on [Travis-"
"CI](http://travis-ci.org/plumed/plumed2), it is possible that aggressive "
"optimization or even architecture dependent features trigger bugs that did "
"not show up on travis. So please always perform the regtests when you "
"install PLUMED."
msgstr ""
"[!attention] [Travis-CI](http://travis-ci.org/plumed/plumed2) "
"で定期テストしていても、強い最適化や Architecture 依存の不具合はあり得ます。インストール時は必ず Regression Test "
"を行ってください。"

#: installation_old.md:442
msgid ""
"Notice that the compiled executable, which now sits in 'src/lib/plumed', "
"relies on other resource files present in the compilation directory. This "
"directory should thus stay in the correct place. One should thus not rename "
"or delete it. In fact the path to the PLUMED root directory is hard coded in"
" the plumed executable as can be verified using"
msgstr ""
"src/lib/plumed はビルド先の Resource に依存するため、Directory を移動・削除しないでください。Root Path "
"は実行ファイルに固定され、次で確認できます。"

#: installation_old.md:452
msgid ""
"In case you try to use the plumed executable without the compilation "
"directory in place (e.g. you move away the src/lib/plumed static executable "
"and delete or rename the compilation directory) PLUMED will not work "
"correctly and will give you an error message"
msgstr "Static 実行ファイルだけ移すなど、ビルド先をなくすと正しく動かずエラーになります。"

#: installation_old.md:462
msgid ""
"You can force plumed to run anyway by using the option `--standalone-"
"executable`:"
msgstr "`--standalone-executable` で強制実行できます。"

#: installation_old.md:468
msgid ""
"Many features will not be available if you run in this way. However, this is"
" currently the only way to use the PLUMED static executable on Windows."
msgstr "多くの機能が使えませんが、Windows で Static 実行ファイルを使う現在唯一の方法です。"

#: installation_old.md:471
msgid "Installing PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED のインストール"

#: installation_old.md:473
msgid ""
"It is strongly suggested to install PLUMED in a predefined location. This is"
" done using"
msgstr "決まった場所へのインストールを強く推奨します。"

#: installation_old.md:481
msgid ""
"This will allow you to remove the original compilation directory, or to "
"recompile a different PLUMED version in the same place."
msgstr "元のビルド先を除去したり、別版のビルドに使ったりできるようになります。"

#: installation_old.md:484
msgid "To install PLUMED one should first decide the location:"
msgstr "まずインストール先を決めます。"

#: installation_old.md:492
msgid ""
"As of PLUMED 2.5 you cannot anymore change the location during install. If "
"you didn't specify the `--prefix` option during configure PLUMED will be "
"installed in `/usr/local`. The install command should be executed with root "
"permissions (e.g. \"sudo make install\") if you want to install PLUMED on a "
"system directory."
msgstr ""
"2.5以降はインストール時に変更できません。configure の `--prefix` 未指定なら `/usr/local` です。System "
"Directory なら sudo make install など Root 権限が必要です。"

#: installation_old.md:497
msgid ""
"Notice that upon installation PLUMED might need to relink a library. This "
"was always true until version 2.1, but in version 2.2 libraries should only "
"be relinked if one changes the install prefix during when typing `make "
"install`. If root user does not have access to compilers, \"sudo -E make "
"install\" might solve the issue."
msgstr ""
"インストール中に Relink が必要な場合があります。2.1までは常に、2.2では `make install` 時に Prefix "
"を変える場合だけです。Root が Compiler にアクセスできないなら sudo -E make install が役立つ場合があります。"

#: installation_old.md:503
msgid ""
"Upon install, the executable is copied to `$prefix/bin`, libraries to "
"`$prefix/lib`, include files to `$prefix/include`, and documentation to "
"`$prefix/shared/doc/plumed`. Additionally, a directory `$prefix/lib/plumed` "
"is created containing several other files, including patch files, object "
"files (for static patches), etc. Notice also that these path can be further "
"customized using standard autoconf directories (e.g. `./configure "
"--bindir=/usr/bin64`)."
msgstr ""
"実行ファイルは `$prefix/bin`、Library は `$prefix/lib`、Include は "
"`$prefix/include`、文書は `$prefix/shared/doc/plumed` に入ります。`$prefix/lib/plumed`"
" に Patch・Object なども置きます。`./configure --bindir=/usr/bin64` など標準 Autoconf "
"Directory でも調整できます。"

#: installation_old.md:511
msgid ""
"One should then set the environment properly. We suggest to do it using the "
"module framework (http://modules.sourceforge.net). An ad hoc generated "
"module file for PLUMED can be found in "
"`$prefix/lib/plumed/src/lib/modulefile` Just edit it as you wish and put it "
"in your modulefile directory. This will also allow you to install multiple "
"PLUMED versions on your machine and to switch among them. If you do not want"
" to use modules, you can still have a look at the modulefile we did so as to"
" know which environment variables should be set for PLUMED to work "
"correctly."
msgstr ""
"環境は Environment Modules (http://modules.sourceforge.net) "
"を推奨します。`$prefix/lib/plumed/src/lib/modulefile` を編集して Module Directory "
"に置けば複数版を切り替えられます。Module を使わなくても必要な環境変数の参考になります。"

#: installation_old.md:520
msgid ""
"If the environment is properly configured one should be able to do the "
"following things:"
msgstr "正しく設定すれば、次ができます。"

#: installation_old.md:523
msgid ""
"use the \"plumed\" executable from the command line. This is also possible "
"before installing."
msgstr "コマンドラインの plumed を使う。インストール前も可能。"

#: installation_old.md:524
msgid ""
"link against the PLUMED library using the \"-lplumed\" flag for the linker. "
"This allows one to use PLUMED library in general purpose programs"
msgstr "-lplumed で Link し、汎用プログラムから使う。"

#: installation_old.md:526
msgid ""
"use PLUMED internal functionality (C++ classes) including header files such "
"as \"#include <plumed/tools/Vector.h>\". This is useful as it may be "
"expedient to exploit the PLUMED library in general purpose programs"
msgstr "#include <plumed/tools/Vector.h> などで C++ Class を利用する。汎用プログラムにも有用。"

#: installation_old.md:530
msgid ""
"As a final note, if you want to install several PLUMED versions without "
"using modules then you should provide a different suffix and/or prefix at "
"configure time:"
msgstr "Module なしで複数版を入れるなら、configure で異なる Prefix・Suffix を指定します。"

#: installation_old.md:538
msgid ""
"This will install a plumed executable named `mpi-plumed_2.2`. All the other "
"files will be renamed similarly, e.g. the PLUMED library will be loaded with"
" `-lmpi-plumed_2.2` and the PLUMED header files will be included with "
"`#include <mpi-plumed_2.2/tools/Vector.h>`. Notice that you can also use "
"arbitrary scripts to edit the name of the executable with the option "
"`--program-transform-name=PROGRAM` (see <a "
"href=\"http://www.gnu.org/software/autoconf/manual/autoconf-2.69/html_node/Transformation-"
"Examples.html#Transformation-Examples\"> autoconf documentation </a> for "
"more info). These options are useful if you do not want to set up modules, "
"but we believe that using modules as described above is more flexible."
msgstr ""
"実行ファイルは `mpi-plumed_2.2`、Link は `-lmpi-plumed_2.2`、Include は `#include <mpi-"
"plumed_2.2/tools/Vector.h>` などになります。`--program-transform-name=PROGRAM` "
"でも名前を編集できます（<a "
"href=\"http://www.gnu.org/software/autoconf/manual/autoconf-2.69/html_node/Transformation-"
"Examples.html#Transformation-Examples\">Autoconf</a>）。便利ですが、Module "
"の方が柔軟だと考えます。"

#: installation_old.md:547
msgid "Patching your MD code"
msgstr "MD コードの Patch"

#: installation_old.md:549
msgid ""
"A growing number of MD codes can use PLUMED without any modification. If you"
" are using one of these codes, refer to its manual to know how to activate "
"PLUMED. In case your MD code is not supporting PLUMED already, you should "
"modify it. We provide scripts to adjust some of the most popular MD codes so"
" as to provide PLUMED support."
msgstr "無変更で対応する MD も増えています。使い方は各マニュアルを参照し、未対応なら提供 Script で変更します。"

#: installation_old.md:555
msgid ""
"You can find information specific for each MD code from the [navigation "
"page](NAVIGATION.md) for this tutorial."
msgstr "コード別の情報は [Navigation](NAVIGATION.md) にあります。"

#: installation_old.md:557
msgid ""
"To patch your MD code, you should have already installed PLUMED properly. "
"This is necessary as you need to have the command \"plumed\" in your "
"execution path. As described above this executable will be in your paths if "
"plumed was installed or if you have run sourceme.sh"
msgstr "Patch には plumed が PATH に必要です。インストールまたは sourceme.sh で準備します。"

#: installation_old.md:562
msgid ""
"Once you have a compiled and working version of plumed, follow these steps "
"to add it to an MD code"
msgstr "動作する版ができたら、"

#: installation_old.md:565
msgid ""
"Configure and compile your MD engine (look for the instructions in its "
"documentation)."
msgstr "MD を文書に従い設定・ビルドする。"

#: installation_old.md:566
msgid "Test if the MD code is working properly."
msgstr "MD が正しく動くかテストする。"

#: installation_old.md:567
msgid "Go to the root directory for the source code of the MD engine."
msgstr "MD Source の Root に移る。"

#: installation_old.md:568
msgid "Patch with PLUMED using:"
msgstr "次で Patch する。"

#: installation_old.md:572
msgid "The script will interactively ask which MD engine you are patching."
msgstr "Script が対話的に MD を尋ねます。"

#: installation_old.md:573
msgid ""
"Once you have patched recompile the MD code (if dependencies are set up "
"properly in the MD engine, only modified files will be recompiled)"
msgstr "Patch 後に再ビルドします。依存が正しければ変更部分だけです。"

#: installation_old.md:576
msgid ""
"There are different options available when patching. You can check all of "
"them using"
msgstr "全オプションは、"

#: installation_old.md:582
msgid "Particularly interesting options include:"
msgstr "特に重要なのは、"

#: installation_old.md:583
msgid ""
"`--static` just link PLUMED as a collection of object files. This is only "
"suggested if for external reasons you absolutely need a static executable. "
"Notice that with this setting it is often more complicated to configure "
"properly the MD code, since all the libraries that PLUMED depends on should "
"be properly specified. The `./configure` script does its best in this sense,"
" but sometime it cannot solve the problem. Additionally, this patching mode "
"has been reported not to work properly on OSX."
msgstr ""
"`--static` は Object File として Link し、Static "
"必須の場合だけ推奨します。全依存の指定で設定が難しく、`./configure` でも解決できない場合や OSX の不具合報告があります。"

#: installation_old.md:588
msgid ""
"`--shared` (default) allows you to link PLUMED as a shared library. As a "
"result when PLUMED is updated, there will be no need to recompile the MD "
"code. This is way better than --static since the libraries that PLUMED "
"depends on should be automatically linked. Notice that if you later remove "
"the directory where PLUMED is installed also the MD code will not run "
"anymore."
msgstr ""
"`--shared` は既定で、更新時の MD 再ビルドが不要、依存も自動 Link されます。ただしインストール先を除くと MD も動きません。"

#: installation_old.md:591
msgid ""
"`--runtime` allows you to choose the location of the PLUMED library at "
"runtime by setting the variable PLUMED_KERNEL. This is probably the most "
"flexible option, and we encourage system administrators to use this option "
"when installing PLUMED on shared facilities. Indeed, using this setting it "
"will be possible to update separately the PLUMED library and the MD code, "
"leaving to the user the possibility to combine different versions at will. "
"We also recommend to use the provided modulefile (see above) to properly set"
" the runtime environment."
msgstr ""
"`--runtime` は PLUMED_KERNEL で実行時に場所を選べ、共有設備に推奨する最も柔軟な方法です。MD と PLUMED "
"を別々に更新し任意に組み合わせられます。付属 Modulefile も推奨します。"

#: installation_old.md:597
msgid ""
"Notice that with PLUMED version <2.5 there was no possibility to link PLUMED"
" as a static library (something like 'libplumed.a'). However, starting with "
"PLUMED 2.5, the `./configure` script will try to set up the system so that a"
" `libplumed.a` file is produced. Patching an MD code with `--static` with "
"try to link against this static library. Creation of the `libplumed.a` "
"library can be avoided with `./configure --disable-static-archive`."
msgstr ""
"2.5未満は Static Library がありません。以降は `./configure` が `libplumed.a` "
"を作り、`--static` で Link します。`libplumed.a` を作らないなら `./configure --disable-"
"static-archive` を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:602
msgid ""
"If your MD code is not supported, you may want to implement an interface for"
" it. Refer to the <a href=\"../../developer-doc/html/index.html\"> developer"
" manual </a>."
msgstr ""
"未対応なら Interface を実装できます。<a href=\"../../developer-"
"doc/html/index.html\">開発者マニュアル</a>を参照してください。"

#: installation_old.md:605
msgid "Cross compiling"
msgstr "Cross-compilation"

#: installation_old.md:607
msgid ""
"If you are compiling an executable from a different machine, then the "
"`plumed` executable will not be available in the compilation environment. "
"This means that you won't be able to perform regtests on the machine nor to "
"compile the manual. You can try to run the regtests on the computing nodes, "
"but this might require some tweak since often machines where people do cross"
" compiling have architectures with limited capabilities on the compute "
"nodes. Also notice that many of the `plumed` options (e.g. patch) are "
"implemented as shell scripts launched from within the `plumed` executable. "
"If the compute nodes have some limitation (e.g. they do not allow to fork "
"new processes) these options will not work. Anyway, the PLUMED library in "
"combination with an MD software should work if both PLUMED and the MD "
"software have been properly compiled."
msgstr ""
"別マシン用の `plumed` はビルド環境で動かず、Test やマニュアル作成はできません。Compute Node で Test "
"するにも制約に合わせた工夫が必要です。`plumed` の patch などは `plumed` 実行ファイル内部から Shell Script "
"を起動するため、Fork 禁止などでは動きません。それでも MD と両方を正しくビルドすれば Library 連携は使えるはずです。"

#: installation_old.md:618
msgid ""
"Also notice that it will not be possible to use the command `plumed patch` "
"on the machine where you are compiling. You should thus use `plumed-patch` "
"instead of `plumed patch` (notice that it should be written as a single "
"word)."
msgstr ""
"ビルド先では `plumed patch` を実行できません。`plumed patch` の代わりに、1語の `plumed-patch` "
"を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:622
msgid "Try e.g.:"
msgstr "例えば、"

#: installation_old.md:628
msgid ""
"This script provides a \"shell only\" implementation of `plumed patch` that "
"will skip the launch of the `plumed` executable."
msgstr "`plumed` 実行ファイルを起動しない、Shell-only の `plumed patch` です。"

#: installation_old.md:630
msgid ""
"Notice that other command line tools will be available in the directory "
"`prefix/lib/progname/`. If configuring with default values this would be "
"`/usr/local/lib/plumed/plumed-*`. These files are not included in the "
"execution path (prefix/bin) to avoid clashes, but can be executed also when "
"plumed is cross compiled and the main plumed executable cannot be launched."
msgstr ""
"ほかのツールは `prefix/lib/progname/`、既定なら `/usr/local/lib/plumed/plumed-*` "
"にあります。衝突防止のため PATH（prefix/bin）には入りませんが、Cross-compile でも実行できます。"

#: installation_old.md:635
msgid "Installing PLUMED on a cluster"
msgstr "Cluster へのインストール"

#: installation_old.md:637
msgid ""
"If you are installing PLUMED on a cluster and you want several users to take"
" advantage of it consider the following suggestions."
msgstr "複数ユーザーで使う場合の助言です。"

#: installation_old.md:640
msgid ""
"First of all, we highly recommend using the module file that PLUMED provides"
" to set up the environment. Just edit it as necessary to make it suitable "
"for your environment."
msgstr "付属 Modulefile を環境に合わせて使うことを強く推奨します。"

#: installation_old.md:643
msgid ""
"Notice that PLUMED can take advantage of many additional features if "
"specific libraries are available upon compiling it."
msgstr "ビルド時に特定 Library があれば多くの追加機能を使えます。"

#: installation_old.md:646
msgid ""
"Try to patch all MD codes with the `--runtime` option. This will allow "
"independent update of PLUMED and MD codes. Users will be able to combine any"
" of the installed gromacs/amber/etc versions with any of the installed "
"PLUMED versions. Notice that it is sometime claimed that statically linked "
"codes are faster. In our experience, this is not true. In case you "
"absolutely need a static executable, be ready to face non trivial linking "
"issues. PLUMED is written in C++, thus required the appropriate C++ library "
"to be linked, and might require additional libraries (e.g. libgsl)."
msgstr ""
"全 MD を `--runtime` で Patch し、独立更新と任意版の組み合わせを可能にしてください。経験上 Static "
"が高速とは限りません。必須なら C++・GSL などの非自明な Link 問題に備えてください。"

#: installation_old.md:652
msgid ""
"Sometime we make small fixes on the patches. For this reason, keep track of "
"which version of PLUMED you used to patch each of the MD code. Perhaps you "
"can call the MD code modules with names such as `gromacs/4.6.7p1`, "
"`gromacs/4.6.7p2` and write somewhere in the module file which version of "
"PLUMED you used. Alternatively, call them something like "
"`gromacs/4.6.7p2.2.0`. In this way, when we report a bug on the mailing "
"list, users will know if the version they are using is affected by it."
msgstr ""
"Patch に小修正が入るため、使用版を記録します。`gromacs/4.6.7p1`・`gromacs/4.6.7p2` と Module "
"に記すか、`gromacs/4.6.7p2.2.0` などにします。不具合報告時に対象か判断できます。"

#: installation_old.md:658
msgid ""
"Usually it is not necessary to install both a MPI and a non-MPI PLUMED "
"version. PLUMED library only calls MPI functions when the MD code is "
"compiled with MPI. PLUMED executable calls MPI functions only when it is "
"invoked without `--no-mpi`. In many machines it is thus sufficient to run "
"the plumed executable on the login node as"
msgstr ""
"通常 MPI・非 MPI の両版は不要です。Library は MD が MPI の場合だけ、実行ファイルは `--no-mpi` なしの場合だけ "
"MPI を呼びます。多くの Login Node では、"

#: installation_old.md:666
msgid ""
"even though PLUMED was compiled with MPI and the login node does not support"
" MPI. The only case where you might need two different PLUMED installation "
"for compute and login node is when you are cross compiling."
msgstr "MPI ビルドでも MPI なしで実行できます。Compute・Login 用に2つ必要なのは主に Cross-compile です。"

#: installation_old.md:670
msgid ""
"PLUMED needs to be well optimized to run efficiently. If you need a single "
"PLUMED binary to run efficiency on machines with different levels of "
"hardware (e.g.: some of your workstations support AVX and some do not), with"
" intel compiler you can use something like"
msgstr "効率には最適化が必要です。AVX 有無など Hardware の異なるマシンで1 Binary を使うには、Intel なら、"

#: installation_old.md:678
msgid ""
"It will take more time to compile but it will allow you to use a single "
"module. Otherwise, you should install two PLUMED version with different "
"optimization levels."
msgstr "ビルドは長くなりますが1 Module にできます。それ以外は最適化レベル別に2版を入れます。"

#: installation_old.md:681
msgid ""
"Using modules, it is not necessary to make the PLUMED module explicitly "
"dependent on the used library. Imagine a scenario where you first installed "
"a module `libgsl`, then load it while you compile PLUMED. If you provide the"
" following option to configure `--enable-rpath`, the PLUMED executable and "
"library will remember where libgsl is, without the need to load libgsl "
"module at runtime. Notice that this trick often does not work for "
"fundamental libraries such as C++ and MPI library. As a consequence, usually"
" the PLUMED module should load the compiler and MPI modules."
msgstr ""
"Module に Library 依存を明示する必要はありません。`libgsl` をロードしてビルドし、`--enable-rpath` "
"を渡すと場所を記憶し、実行時の GSL Module は不要です。ただし C++・MPI など基本 Library では使えないことが多く、通常その "
"Module はロードします。"

#: installation_old.md:688
msgid ""
"[!attention] In case you found out how to compile PLUMED on some fancy "
"architecture please share your tricks! You can either post it in your blog, "
"send it to the mailing list, or ask as to update this paragraph in the "
"manual, we will be happy to do so."
msgstr ""
"[!attention] 特殊 Architecture のビルドに成功したら、Blog・Mailing "
"List、マニュアル更新依頼などで方法を共有してください。"

#: installation_old.md:693
msgid "Installing Python wrappers"
msgstr "Python Wrapper のインストール"

#: installation_old.md:695
msgid ""
"As of PLUMED 2.5 it is possible to use the PLUMED library through Python "
"wrappers. Notice that this is not something for end users but rather for "
"developers. The interface is very similar to the one used in MD codes linked"
" with PLUMED."
msgstr "2.5以降は Python Wrapper を使えます。主に開発者向けで、MD Interface とよく似ています。"

#: installation_old.md:697
msgid "There are two ways to install Python wrappers."
msgstr "方法は2つです。"

#: installation_old.md:699
msgid "Installing Python wrappers within PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED 内へのインストール"

#: installation_old.md:701
msgid ""
"If `./configure` finds a `python` executable that also has the `cython` "
"module available, Python wrappers will be installed within "
"`/prefix/lib/plumed/python`. In order to access them, you should add this "
"directory to the environment variable `PYTHONPATH`. Notice that if your "
"python interpreter has a different name you might have to pass it to "
"`./configure` with `PYTHON_BIN=python3.6`. The whole thing would then be:"
msgstr ""
"`./configure` が `cython` のある `python` を見つけると `/prefix/lib/plumed/python` "
"に入れます。`PYTHONPATH` に追加してください。別名なら `./configure` に `PYTHON_BIN=python3.6` "
"を渡します。全手順は、"

#: installation_old.md:711
msgid ""
"Notice that in this manner you will have to commit to a specific python "
"version **before** installing PLUMED."
msgstr "この方法は PLUMED のインストール __前__ に Python 版を決める必要があります。"

#: installation_old.md:713
msgid "Installing Python wrappers outside PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED 外へのインストール"

#: installation_old.md:715
msgid ""
"If you use multiple python versions, you might find it easier to install the"
" Python wrappers separately from PLUMED. The simplest way is to do it with "
"`pip`:"
msgstr "複数 Python なら別に入れる方が便利です。最も簡単には `pip` を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:721
msgid ""
"Here the `--user` flag allows you to install the packages on your home. "
"Notice that you don't even need to download PLUMED in order to install the "
"wrappers, but you will need PLUMED in order to use them. You can tell the "
"wrappers where PLUMED is by setting the `PLUMED_KERNEL` environment "
"variable:"
msgstr ""
"`--user` は Home に入れます。Wrapper の導入だけなら PLUMED "
"取得は不要ですが、使用には必要です。`PLUMED_KERNEL` で場所を指定します。"

#: installation_old.md:729
msgid ""
"Notice that by installing the wrappers in this manner you will download "
"those that are packaged on [Pypi](https://pypi.org/project/plumed/). If you "
"want to install using pip the development version of the wrappers you should"
" download the PLUMED repository and use the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"この方法は [PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/plumed/) 版です。開発版ならリポジトリを取得し、次を使います。"

#: installation_old.md:740
msgid ""
"If you want to install the development version it is recommended to use a "
"virtualenv so that it will not interfere with the released packages."
msgstr "開発版は Release と干渉しない virtualenv を推奨します。"

#: installation_old.md:742
msgid "Other hints"
msgstr "その他の助言"

#: installation_old.md:744
msgid ""
"We here collect a list of suggestions that might be useful on particular "
"machines."
msgstr "特定マシンで有用な情報です。"

#: installation_old.md:747
msgid ""
"On Blue Gene Q (likely on AIX) the prelinking made with `ld -r` is not "
"working properly. There is no easy way to detect this at configure time. If "
"during `make` you receive an error in the form"
msgstr ""
"Blue Gene Q（おそらく AIX）では `ld -r` の Prelink が動かず、自動検出も困難です。`make` で次のエラーなら、"

#: installation_old.md:753
msgid "please configure plumed again with the following flag"
msgstr "次の Flag で再設定します。"

#: installation_old.md:757
msgid ""
"On Cray machines, you might have to set the following environment variable "
"before configuring and building both PLUMED and the MD code that you want to"
" patch with PLUMED (kindly reported by Marco De La Pierre):"
msgstr ""
"Cray では PLUMED と対象 MD の設定・ビルド前に次の環境変数が必要な場合があります（Marco De La Pierre の報告）。"

#: installation_old.md:763
msgid ""
"Intel MPI seems to require the flags `-lmpi_mt -mt_mpi` for compiling and "
"linking and the flag `-DMPICH_IGNORE_CXX_SEEK` for compiling (kindly "
"reported by Abhishek Acharya). You might want to try to configure using"
msgstr ""
"Intel MPI は Compile・Link に `-lmpi_mt -mt_mpi`、Compile に "
"`-DMPICH_IGNORE_CXX_SEEK` が必要なようです（Abhishek Acharya の報告）。次を試せます。"

#: installation_old.md:769
msgid ""
"Adding libraries to `STATIC_LIBS` uses them for all the linking steps, "
"whereas those in `LIBS` are only used when linking the PLUMED kernel "
"library. See more at [this thread](https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/plumed-"
"users/CAB1aw3y0m%3D5qwzsZY4ZB-"
"aBevsL5iuS%3DmQuSWK_cw527zCMqzg%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&utm_source=footer)."
msgstr ""
"`STATIC_LIBS` は全 Link 段階、`LIBS` は Kernel Library の Link "
"だけに使います。[議論](https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/plumed-"
"users/CAB1aw3y0m%3D5qwzsZY4ZB-"
"aBevsL5iuS%3DmQuSWK_cw527zCMqzg%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&utm_source=footer)"
" を参照してください。"
